   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} \\frac{(x + 1)^{2} - 9}{x - 2} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 6
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x + 1 \\). As \\( x \\to 2 \\), \\( u \\to 3 \\), and \\( x - 2 = u - 3 \\), so the numerator is \\( g(u) - g(3) \\) with \\( g(u) = u^{2} \\) and \\( g(3) = 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": 9
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( g(u) = u^{2} \\) and the base point is \\( u = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is \\( \\lim_{u \\to 3} \\frac{g(u) - g(3)}{u - 3} = g'(3) \\), and \\( g'(u) = 2 u \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "u"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( g'(3) = 6 \\).",
         "mathjson": 6
      }
   ],
